#: ../../tools/cath_tools.rst:90 c40384d3917845bb90d99ca749fe5f00
msgid ""
"Get CATH protein structure superfamily information by CATH ID. CATH "
"classifies protein domain str..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/cath_tools.rst 626af2e819dc48389ec9e4bbdbfcc47e
msgid "CATH_get_superfamily tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/cath_tools.rst:96 a79cb7b787424aa182ba4a67d75ef831
msgid "**Name**: ``CATH_get_superfamily``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/cath_tools.rst:98 dff2796676d4492995ee6fee17d33bc4
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get CATH protein structure superfamily information by "
"CATH ID. CATH classifies protein domain structures into a four-level "
"hierarchy: Class, Architecture, Topology, Homologous superfamily. "
"Superfamilies group evolutionarily related domains. Returns "
"classification name, number of families, and domain counts. Example: "
"2.40.50.140 returns 'Nucleic acid-binding proteins' with 227 S35 families"
" and 2,879 total domains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/cath_tools.rst:102 dd4ef65a65df4f03a8ac76cc8b791f61
msgid ""
"``superfamily_id`` (string) (required) CATH superfamily ID in C.A.T.H "
"format. Examples: '2.40.50.140' (Nucleic acid-binding proteins), "
"'3.40.50.300' (P-loop NTPases), '1.10.510.10' (Globin-like), '2.60.40.10'"
" (Immunoglobulin-like)."
msgstr ""

